# kk: Several timestamp query pools share a counter heap
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46190 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

KK creates its own Metal counter heap for each timestamp query pool, and Metal limits how many a process can have.

When it reaches the limit, vkCreateQueryPool fails with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY and Metal reports "too many heaps".

Now the pools are distributed inside shared heaps of 4096 entries (up to 64 heaps). If a pool does not fit, it uses its own heap as before.

This was identified in a PS5 emulator, which creates timestamp pools while running normally. The following was tested:

* Minimal test: 32 pools and then the error, versus 2000 of 2000.
* CTS: 2,266 timestamp, query_pool and multiview queries tests, same results with and without the change, 0 failures.
* Game in a PS5 emulator: 1,205 and 17,625 "too many heaps" errors per run without the change, 0 with it.
* Hardware: M5 Pro, macOS 27.3.

Assisted-by: LLM

